 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the query parser only matching 'none' (uppercase) for unassigned tasks, rejecting lowercase 'none'. The fix converts the assignee_id value to lowercase before comparison, ensuring both 'None' and 'none' are treated as unassigned tasks. This resolves the validation error and correctly returns unassigned tasks.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/query.py b/tracker/query.py\nindex d765032..0117662 100644\n--- a/tracker/query.py\n+++ b/tracker/query.py\n@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ def build_filters(params, now_iso=None):\n         args.extend(statuses)\n     assignee = params.get(\"assignee_id\")\n     if assignee is not None and assignee != \"\":\n-        if str(assignee) == \"none\":\n+        if str(assignee).lower() == 'none':\n             clauses.append(\"assignee_id IS NULL\")\n         else:\n             clauses.append(\"assignee_id = ?\")\n",
